libmount: preserve child semantics with callback clone on wasm

External mount helpers and mount -a -F have bounded child continuations, so
run those continuations with callback clone on wasm while retaining the native
fork paths.  The shared worker exit maps libmount state to mount(8) status;
this also fixes native -F overlooking an external helper failure when the raw
mnt_context_mount() call itself succeeded.  The exported generic double-return
mnt_fork_context API remains unsupported because a callback cannot represent
that contract.  Idmapped USER_NS creation remains unavailable because user
namespaces are not configured.

